       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose is unsafe as written.\n\n- Acetaminophen 2000 mg three times daily comes to **6,000 mg/day**. The usual adult maximum is **4,000 mg/day**, and many institutions cap it at 3,000 mg/day.\n- A single 2,000 mg dose is also twice the usual maximum single dose of 1,000 mg.\n- At 6 g/day, the risk of hepatotoxicity is significant, even with normal liver function.\n\nHere are some standard options for a 70 kg adult with normal renal and hepatic function:\n1. **1000 mg PO every 8 hours** (3 times daily, 3 g/day).\n2. **1000 mg PO every 6 hours** (4 times daily, 4 g/day, the maximum).\n3. **650 mg PO every 6 hours** (4 times daily, 2.6 g/day).\n\nDid you mean one of these, for example 1000 mg three times daily? Or is there a reason for the higher dose that I should know about? Once you confirm the dose and frequency, I'll enter the order."
